    ]
  },
  {
    title: "Developer ID transcript options",
    rows: [
      ["--locale <identifier>", "Transcribe with a specific locale. Defaults to the current locale."],
      ["--output <file>", "Write transcript output to a file instead of stdout."],
      ["--semantic-turns", "Use automatic turn grouping."],
      ["--diarize", "Identify and label speakers with Luxel's bundled local diarization model."],
      ["--json", "Print full transcript JSON instead of plain text."],
      ["--overwrite", "Replace the transcript output file if it already exists."]
    ]
  },
  {
    title: "Result and callback options",
    rows: [
      ["--wait", "Wait for Luxel to call back with the command result."],
      ["--json", "Wait for the result and print JSON."],
      ["--timeout <seconds>", "Set callback wait time. The default is 120 seconds."],
      ["--print-url, --dry-run", "Print the Luxel automation URL instead of opening it."],
      ["--x-success <url>", "Callback URL for successful execution. File results append filePath; recording starts append recordingID."],
      ["--x-error <url>", "Callback URL for failed execution. Failures append errorMessage."],
      ["--help", "Show help for the current command."]
    ]
  }
];

const supportedLocales = [
  "English",
  "German",
  "Spanish",
  "French",
  "Italian",
  "Japanese",
  "Korean",
  "Vietnamese",
  "Simplified Chinese",
  "Portuguese (Brazil)",
  "Portuguese (Portugal)"
];

const troubleshooting = [
  { problem: "Luxel keeps asking for screen permission", answer: "Make sure you are opening the same copy of Luxel each time. After changing Screen & System Audio Recording access, quit and reopen Luxel." },
  { problem: "Record buttons are disabled", answer: "Choose a capture target and resolve the visible permission chips. Screen capture needs Screen & System Audio Recording permission; audio-only capture needs microphone permission." },
  { problem: "Screen capture still fails after allowing permission", answer: "Quit and reopen Luxel after changing Screen & System Audio Recording access. If Luxel still is not listed, remove old Luxel entries from the permission list and open Luxel again." },
  { problem: "Microphone audio is missing", answer: "Enable Record Microphone, choose a valid microphone or System Default, and grant Microphone permission. GIF and APNG exports do not carry audio." },
  { problem: "Quick Record is disabled", answer: "Create or select a quick export preset, then choose a target or enable Remember Last Capture so Luxel has a previous capture to repeat." },
  { problem: "Copy Frame or Save Frame As is disabled", answer: "Pause preview playback first. Frame grabs use the current paused frame and save as PNG." },
  { problem: "Shortcut does not fire", answer: "Make sure Keyboard Shortcuts is enabled, remove duplicate shortcuts, and avoid known macOS capture shortcuts, including:", shortcuts: systemShortcutConflicts },
  { problem: "The notch controls are not visible", answer: "Luxel uses the built-in notch when a notched display is detected and the Notch setting is enabled. Otherwise it falls back to the floating HUD if that fallback is enabled, or to menu-bar-only status." },
  { problem: "Replay buffer cannot start", answer: "Enable Replay Buffer, grant Screen & System Audio Recording permission, and make sure a normal recording is not already active. Luxel pauses the buffer while regular recordings run." },
  { problem: "Replay buffer clips are shorter than requested", answer: "The buffer can only export captured history that already exists. Wait until the menu reports that replay buffering is active before clipping the full selected duration." },
  { problem: "The luxel command is not found", answer: "Open Settings > Command Line, install or repair the command, then copy the PATH command for your shell if the install directory is not already on PATH." },
  { problem: "Developer ID CLI transcription fails", answer: "Confirm speech recognition is available and authorized, then retry. The transcribe command uses local transcription, the selected locale, and the same speech recognition availability as the app." }
];
---

<PageLayout
  title="Luxel Documentation"
  description="Luxel user documentation for installation, permissions, capture, replay buffer, editing, export, transcripts, command-line control, automation, localization, settings, and troubleshooting."
  bodyClass="docs-page"
  navigationLabel="Documentation navigation"
  showsLeftGlow
>

    <main class="docs-layout">
      <aside class="docs-sidebar" aria-label="Documentation sections">
        <nav>
          {navGroups.map((group) => (
            <div class="docs-nav-group">
              <p>{group.title}</p>
              {group.links.map((link) => <a href={link.href}>{link.label}</a>)}
            </div>
          ))}
        </nav>
      </aside>

      <div class="docs-content">
        <section class="docs-hero" id="overview" aria-labelledby="overview-title">
          <p class="docs-eyebrow">Luxel Docs</p>
          <h1 class="gradient-title" id="overview-title">Use Luxel from first launch to final export.</h1>
          <p class="docs-lead">
            Luxel is a Mac menu bar recorder for screen capture, area capture,
            replay buffer clips, audio-only recordings, camera preview overlays,
            local transcripts, command-line automation, quick exports, and editor-based exports.
          </p>

          <div class="docs-hero-grid">
            <article>
              <h2>Start in three steps</h2>
              <ol>
                <li>Launch Luxel and find it in the menu bar.</li>
                <li>Grant only the permissions needed for the capture you are about to make.</li>
                <li>Pick a target, record, then open the result in the editor or Finder.</li>
              </ol>
            </article>

            <article>
              <h2>Capture from the app, buffer, or scripts</h2>
              <p>
                Use the menu bar for interactive recording, global shortcuts for repeated
                actions, Replay Buffer for the moments that already happened, and the{" "}
                <code>luxel</code> command for scripted captures.
              </p>
            </article>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="docs-section" id="install" aria-labelledby="install-title">
          <div class="section-heading">
            <p class="docs-eyebrow">Setup</p>
            <h2 id="install-title">Installation and first launch</h2>
          </div>

          <div class="split-grid">
            <article>
              <h3>Install Luxel</h3>
              <ol>
                <li>Install and launch Luxel.</li>
                <li>Keep the app in a stable location before granting permissions.</li>
                <li>Open Luxel from Finder or Launchpad.</li>
                <li>Look for the Luxel status item in the macOS menu bar.</li>
              </ol>
              <p class="note">
                Current builds require macOS 26.0 or later. Luxel runs from the menu bar,
                so the menu bar item is the main place to start captures and open settings.
              </p>
            </article>

            <article>
              <h3>First capture</h3>
              <ol>
                <li>Open Luxel from the menu bar.</li>
                <li>Choose a target from Target, or use Area to draw a custom region.</li>
                <li>Enable System Audio, Microphone, or Camera only if the recording needs them.</li>
                <li>Click Record Source, Record Area, or Record Audio.</li>
                <li>Stop recording from the menu bar status controls, active recording controls, or shortcut.</li>
              </ol>
            </article>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="docs-section" id="permissions" aria-labelledby="permissions-title">
          <div class="section-heading">
            <p class="docs-eyebrow">Privacy</p>
            <h2 id="permissions-title">Permissions</h2>
            <p>
              Luxel requests permissions only when a feature needs them. Permission chips
              appear in the menu when a required permission is missing.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="permission-grid">
            <article>
              <h3>Screen & System Audio Recording</h3>
              <p>
                Required for display, window, area, and system-audio capture.
                macOS may label this setting as Screen & System Audio Recording in
                System Settings > Privacy & Security.
              </p>
              <p class="expected">After granting access, quit and reopen Luxel.</p>
            </article>

            <article>
              <h3>Microphone</h3>
              <p>
                Required when Record Microphone is on, when the area picker microphone
                toggle is on, or when you start an audio-only recording.
              </p>
              <p class="expected">You can choose System Default or a specific input device.</p>
            </article>

            <article>
              <h3>Camera</h3>
              <p>
                Required when camera preview is enabled. Luxel uses the selected camera
                to show a floating preview overlay for recordings.
              </p>
              <p class="expected">Camera controls appear after you choose a camera device.</p>
            </article>

            <article>
              <h3>Speech Recognition</h3>
              <p>
                Required when generating local transcripts in the editor or from the
                command line. Luxel uses on-device speech recognition for transcription.
              </p>
              <p class="expected">Luxel asks for this only when transcription starts.</p>
            </article>
          </div>

          <div class="callout">
            <h3>Permission tip</h3>
            <p>
              After changing Screen & System Audio Recording access, quit and reopen Luxel.
              If macOS keeps prompting, make sure you are opening the same copy of Luxel
              each time.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="docs-section" id="concepts" aria-labelledby="concepts-title">
          <div class="section-heading">
            <p class="docs-eyebrow">Model</p>
            <h2 id="concepts-title">Core concepts</h2>
          </div>

          <div class="concept-list">
            <article>
              <h3>Menu bar first</h3>
              <p>
                Luxel lives in the menu bar. The panel contains target selection,
                capture buttons, audio toggles, permission status, recent files,
                replay controls, and settings access.
              </p>
            </article>
            <article>
              <h3>Targets</h3>
              <p>
                A target can be a display, an app window, or a selected area. Active-window
                and fullscreen commands resolve their target at the moment capture starts.
              </p>
            </article>
            <article>
              <h3>Recordings folder</h3>
              <p>
                New recordings default to <code>~/Movies/Luxel</code>. You can choose a different
                folder in Output settings.
              </p>
            </article>
            <article>
              <h3>Editor</h3>
              <p>
                Standard video recordings open in the editor after capture. Audio-only
                recordings can open in the editor for playback, transcript review, and
                audio export. Quick exports can finish directly to a file or post-action.
              </p>
            </article>
            <article>
              <h3>Quick exports</h3>
              <p>
                Export presets can turn a capture into GIF, MP4, HEVC MP4,
                ProRes MOV, or APNG output without manually opening every export control.
              </p>
            </article>
            <article>
              <h3>Replay buffer</h3>
              <p>
                Replay Buffer is an opt-in rolling capture mode. It keeps recent screen
                history available so you can export the last selected duration as a normal
                MP4 recording.
              </p>
            </article>
            <article>
              <h3>Local transcripts</h3>
              <p>
                Luxel transcribes audio on your Mac. Local speaker identification can
                diarize conversations, match Known Speakers, and label transcript turns.
                Transcripts can stay in the editor workflow or be written from the CLI
                as text or JSON.
              </p>
            </article>
            <article>
              <h3>Recent files</h3>
              <p>
                The menu shows the latest recording and a Recent menu for opening clips
                in the editor or revealing them in Finder.
              </p>
            </article>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="docs-section" id="capture" aria-labelledby="capture-title">
          <div class="section-heading">
            <p class="docs-eyebrow">Guide</p>
            <h2 id="capture-title">Capture guide</h2>
          </div>

          <div class="guide-stack">
            <article>
              <h3>Record a screen, window, or area</h3>
              <ol>
                <li>Open Luxel from the menu bar.</li>
                <li>Choose Target and select a display or window.</li>
                <li>Turn on System Audio or Microphone if needed.</li>
                <li>Click Record Source, or use Record Area for a selected region.</li>
                <li>Use Stop, Pause, or Resume from the recording controls.</li>
              </ol>
              <p class="tip">Audio-only recordings do not support pause and resume.</p>
            </article>

            <article>
              <h3>Tune capture behavior</h3>
              <ul>
                <li>Choose a fixed screen recording rate from 1 to 120 FPS, or match the display refresh rate.</li>
                <li>Choose whether the cursor is visible and whether clicks are highlighted.</li>
                <li>Enable system audio, microphone audio, or both before recording.</li>
                <li>Use countdown and auto-stop when a capture needs a timed start or end.</li>
              </ul>
            </article>

            <article>
              <h3>Record audio only</h3>
              <ol>
                <li>Grant Microphone permission.</li>
                <li>Choose System Default or a specific input device in Recording settings.</li>
                <li>Choose AAC or ALAC as the audio-only format.</li>
                <li>Click Audio in the menu bar or use the Audio Only shortcut.</li>
              </ol>
              <p class="tip">Audio-only files use the <code>.m4a</code> extension.</p>
            </article>

            <article>
              <h3>Add camera preview</h3>
              <ol>
                <li>Open Recording settings or the area picker camera menu.</li>
                <li>Choose a camera device and grant Camera permission.</li>
                <li>Choose Squircle, Rounded, or Square shape.</li>
                <li>Optionally enable Cutout to isolate the presenter or Green Screen to remove a chroma-key background.</li>
                <li>Choose the overlay size and mirror behavior.</li>
                <li>Position the floating preview before or during setup.</li>
              </ol>
              <p class="tip">
                The floating preview appears in the recording when it overlaps the
                capture target.
              </p>
            </article>

            <article>
              <h3>Use countdown and auto-stop</h3>
              <p>
                The area picker supports countdown presets of Off, 3 seconds, 5 seconds,
                and 10 seconds. Stop-after presets include Off, 10 seconds, 30 seconds,
                1 minute, 5 minutes, and a custom duration from 0:01 to 12:00:00.
              </p>
              <p class="tip">Stopping during countdown cancels the countdown instead of saving a recording.</p>
            </article>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="docs-section" id="replay-buffer" aria-labelledby="replay-buffer-title">
          <div class="section-heading">
            <p class="docs-eyebrow">Guide</p>
            <h2 id="replay-buffer-title">Clip what just happened</h2>
            <p>
              Replay Buffer continuously keeps recent screen history available while it is active.
              It is opt-in, visible in the menu bar, and uses the same Screen & System Audio
              Recording permission as normal screen capture.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="split-grid">
            <article>
              <h3>Set up Replay Buffer</h3>
              <ol>
                <li>Open Settings > Replay Buffer.</li>
                <li>Enable Replay Buffer and approve the first-use consent prompt.</li>
                <li>Choose a length: 30 seconds, 1 minute, 2 minutes, or 5 minutes.</li>
                <li>Choose 24 FPS or 30 FPS.</li>
                <li>Turn on Include System Audio only when clips need Mac audio.</li>
                <li>Choose whether clips open in the editor or use the quick export destination.</li>
              </ol>
            </article>

            <article>
              <h3>Use it from the menu</h3>
              <ol>
                <li>Start Replay Buffer from the menu bar control.</li>
                <li>Wait until the status moves from starting to buffering.</li>
                <li>Click Export to save the selected recent duration.</li>
                <li>Use Start and Stop to arm or disarm the buffer.</li>
                <li>Use the Clip Replay Buffer shortcut or <code>luxel clip</code> for the same action.</li>
              </ol>
            </article>
          </div>

          <div class="guide-stack">
            <article>
              <h3>Behavior and privacy</h3>
              <ul>
                <li>Replay Buffer captures the display with cursor and stores temporary segment files in Luxel's cache while active.</li>
                <li>Normal recordings pause the replay buffer and it resumes when recording stops.</li>
                <li>The buffer pauses for system reasons such as display sleep, lock, battery, or display changes.</li>
                <li>Resume on Launch is off unless you enable it in Replay Buffer settings.</li>
                <li>Clips are MP4 files named like <code>Luxel Replay 2026-07-01 at 14.30.00.mp4</code>.</li>
              </ul>
              <p class="tip">
                If you clip before enough history exists, Luxel saves the available portion rather than inventing missing time.
              </p>
            </article>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="docs-section" id="cropper" aria-labelledby="cropper-title">
          <div class="section-heading">
            <p class="docs-eyebrow">Area Picker</p>
            <h2 id="cropper-title">Select and refine an area</h2>
          </div>

          <div class="split-grid">
            <article>
              <h3>Draw a selection</h3>
              <p>
                Click Area to open the full-screen selection overlay. Drag to draw a
                region, resize it with handles, or use Full Display to select the display.
                The minimum selection is 32 by 32 pixels.
              </p>
              <p>
                Size presets include 1280 by 720, 1920 by 1080, and 800 by 600.
                Aspect ratio choices include Free, 16:9, 4:3, 1:1, 9:16, and 21:9.
              </p>
            </article>

            <article>
              <h3>Useful controls</h3>
              <ul>
                <li>Choose countdown, stop-after, audio, camera, ratio, and size controls.</li>
                <li>Toggle microphone and camera when permissions allow it.</li>
                <li>Use the loupe for precise edges.</li>
                <li>Dim other displays or restore the last selection from Presets settings.</li>
                <li>Open Focus settings from the notification reminder if you want fewer interruptions.</li>
              </ul>
            </article>
          </div>

          <div class="mini-reference">
            <h3>Area picker shortcuts and gestures</h3>
            <table>
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th>Input</th>
                  <th>Action</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                {areaPickerShortcuts.map((shortcut) => (
                  <tr>
                    <td>
                      <ShortcutKeys keys={shortcut.keys} />
                    </td>
                    <td>{shortcut.action}</td>
                  </tr>
                ))}
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="docs-section" id="editor" aria-labelledby="editor-title">
          <div class="section-heading">
            <p class="docs-eyebrow">Guide</p>
            <h2 id="editor-title">Edit and export recordings</h2>
          </div>

          <div class="guide-stack">
            <article>
              <h3>Open and review</h3>
              <p>
                After a standard video recording stops, Luxel opens the editor with a
                preview, source filename, duration, dimensions, audio status, alpha status,
                estimated file size, Save Original, and Export controls.
              </p>
              <p>
                Rename the source file in place, move to newer or older recordings in the
                same folder. Developer ID builds can also open an existing media file with{" "}
                <code>luxel editor &lt;file&gt;</code>.
              </p>
            </article>

            <article>
              <h3>Trim, resize, and retime</h3>
              <ul>
                <li>Use Timeline start and end controls to trim the output range.</li>
                <li>Choose Original, percentage size presets, or Custom width and height.</li>
                <li>Use Crop to Fill when fitting the output size.</li>
                <li>Set frame rate and playback speed from 0.1x to 10x.</li>
                <li>Preview playback loops inside the trim range.</li>
              </ul>
            </article>

            <article>
              <h3>Choose export formats</h3>
              <table>
                <thead>
                  <tr>
                    <th>Format</th>
                    <th>Notes</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  <tr>
                    <td>MP4 (H.264)</td>
                    <td>Most-compatible video export with Compact, Balanced, or High quality.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td>MP4 (HEVC)</td>
                    <td>Smaller-file HEVC export with Compact, Balanced, or High quality.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td>MOV (ProRes 422)</td>
                    <td>Editing and mastering export with fixed High quality and LPCM audio.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td>MOV (ProRes 4444)</td>
                    <td>High-fidelity ProRes export with fixed High quality and LPCM audio.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td>GIF</td>
                    <td>Animated image export. Audio is dropped. Supports loop and dithering options.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td>APNG</td>
                    <td>Lossless animated PNG export. Audio is dropped.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td>WebM (VP9)</td>
                    <td>WebM export with Compact, Balanced, or High quality.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td>MP4 (AV1)</td>
                    <td>AV1 MP4 export with AAC audio through the bundled SVT-AV1 encoder.</td>
                  </tr>
                </tbody>
              </table>
              <p class="tip">
                The format menu can select multiple formats and shows size estimates when
                Luxel can calculate them. MP4, MOV, WebM, and AV1 exports use even pixel dimensions.
              </p>
            </article>

            <article>
              <h3>Adjust audio</h3>
              <ul>
                <li>Use Include Audio to mute or keep audio for formats that support it.</li>
                <li>Set audio level from 0% to 200%.</li>
                <li>Enable Normalize Audio to smooth loudness during export.</li>
                <li>Audio-only sources export as M4A, ALAC M4A, WAV, CAF, or FLAC.</li>
              </ul>
              <p class="tip">GIF and APNG always drop audio.</p>
            </article>

            <article>
              <h3>Export actions</h3>
              <p>
                During export, Luxel shows progress and lets you cancel. After export,
                actions include Open, Reveal in Finder, Save a Copy, Open With, Copy File,
                Copy Path, and Share. Multi-format export creates a batch folder named
                after the source recording.
              </p>
              <p class="tip">
                Copy Frame and Save Frame As use the current paused frame and save PNG output.
              </p>
            </article>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="docs-section" id="transcripts" aria-labelledby="transcripts-title">
          <div class="section-heading">
            <p class="docs-eyebrow">Guide</p>
            <h2 id="transcripts-title">Create local transcripts</h2>
            <p>
              Luxel uses local transcription for recordings with audio. Use the editor for review
              workflows. Developer ID builds also provide transcript files from the CLI for scripts.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="callout">
            <h3>For the clearest transcripts</h3>
            <p>
              Use headphones or AirPods when recording System Audio and Microphone together.
              Mac speakers can feed the same audio back into the mic, creating duplicate text
              across both sources and reducing transcription and speaker-label accuracy.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="split-grid">
            <article>
              <h3>In the editor</h3>
              <ol>
                <li>Open a recording with audio in the editor.</li>
                <li>Use the transcript preview to generate or review transcript text.</li>
                <li>Search transcript text or select transcript spans to jump playback.</li>
                <li>Leave Segment Transcript Turns enabled for automatic turn grouping.</li>
                <li>Turn it off in Settings > Transcripts for faster raw transcripts on long recordings.</li>
              </ol>
            </article>

            <article>
              <h3>Identify and manage speakers</h3>
              <ol>
                <li>Enable Identify Speakers in Settings > Transcripts.</li>
                <li>Generate a transcript to separate and label each detected voice locally.</li>
                <li>In the Speakers card, use Auto detection or set an Exact speaker count or Range, then re-run detection.</li>
                <li>Play voice examples, name a detected speaker, save it as a Known Speaker, attach it to an existing profile, or ignore it.</li>
                <li>Future transcripts can match saved Known Speakers automatically.</li>
              </ol>
              <p class="tip">Voice profiles and speaker processing stay on your Mac.</p>
            </article>

            <article>
              <h3>From the command line (Developer ID)</h3>
              <pre><code>luxel transcribe demo.m4a &gt; demo.txt
luxel transcribe demo.mp4 --output demo.json --json --overwrite
luxel transcribe demo.mp4 --locale en_US --semantic-turns --diarize</code></pre>
              <p class="tip">
                Plain text is printed to stdout by default. Use <code>--json</code> for
                full turn-segmented transcript data, including speaker labels when
                {" "}<code>--diarize</code> is enabled.
              </p>
            </article>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="docs-section" id="workflows" aria-labelledby="workflows-title">
          <div class="section-heading">
            <p class="docs-eyebrow">Workflows</p>
            <h2 id="workflows-title">Compound workflows</h2>
          </div>

          <div class="workflow-grid">
            <article>
              <h3>Capture, refine, export, share</h3>
              <ol>
                <li>Record a display, window, or area.</li>
                <li>Stop to open the editor.</li>
                <li>Trim the range, choose size, frame rate, and speed.</li>
                <li>Export as MP4, HEVC, ProRes MOV, GIF, APNG, WebM, or AV1.</li>
                <li>Use Copy Path, Share, or Reveal in Finder from the exported file menu.</li>
              </ol>
            </article>

            <article>
              <h3>Fast GIF from a selected area</h3>
              <ol>
                <li>Create an export preset with GIF format and the desired destination.</li>
                <li>Set it as the Quick Recording preset.</li>
                <li>
                  Open Area, draw a selection, and press
                  <span class="shortcut-keys--inline">
                    <ShortcutKeys keys={["option", "click"]} />
                  </span>
                  Record.
                </li>
                <li>Let the preset run its post-action after capture.</li>
              </ol>
            </article>

            <article>
              <h3>Repeat a previous capture</h3>
              <ol>
                <li>Turn on Remember Last Capture in Presets settings.</li>
                <li>Make a normal capture once.</li>
                <li>Use Quick Record Last from the shortcut, CLI, URL automation, or App Shortcut.</li>
                <li>For a new selected area, use the area picker's Quick Record action with the active quick preset.</li>
              </ol>
            </article>

            <article>
              <h3>Replay a bug after it happens</h3>
              <ol>
                <li>Enable Replay Buffer before the session starts.</li>
                <li>Choose a 1 minute, 2 minute, or 5 minute length based on how much history you need.</li>
                <li>When the issue appears, click Export or run <code>luxel clip --seconds 30 --wait</code>.</li>
                <li>Open the clip in the editor or let the quick export destination handle it.</li>
              </ol>
            </article>

            <article>
              <h3>Paused-frame handoff</h3>
              <ol>
                <li>Open a recording in the editor.</li>
                <li>Pause on the frame you need.</li>
                <li>Use Copy Frame or Save Frame As from the editor actions.</li>
                <li>Use the saved PNG or clipboard image in the destination app.</li>
              </ol>
            </article>

            <article>
              <h3>Scripted export and transcript (Developer ID)</h3>
              <ol>
                <li>Install the command from Settings > Command Line.</li>
                <li>Run <code>luxel convert demo.mp4 demo.webm --width 1280 --height 720</code>.</li>
                <li>Use <code>luxel convert demo.mp4 demo-av1.mp4 --format av1</code> when you want MP4 AV1.</li>
                <li>Run <code>luxel transcribe demo.mp4 --output demo.txt</code>.</li>
                <li>Use <code>--json</code> when another tool needs structured output.</li>
              </ol>
            </article>
          </div>
        </section>

